1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,700
Classroom two sits a short drive
away, in Hitler's birthplace,

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:06,240
and it's where our
half-read declaration lives.

3
00:00:06,980 --> 00:00:11,080
After 1945, Austria's official
memory rested on paragraph one:

4
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:13,080
annexed, not complicit.

5
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:18,240
Studies of Austrian textbooks
report that, until the 1970s,

6
00:00:18,460 --> 00:00:21,620
the Holocaust hardly appeared
in them, and when it did,

7
00:00:22,020 --> 00:00:25,320
it could look like Hitler's private
crime, brought in from Germany.

8
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:26,160
Hang on.

9
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:27,760
Hitler was born in Austria.

10
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:29,980
Not according to those textbooks, teacher.

11
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:34,220
According to those, he just moved
away and came back with an army.

12
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:40,600
The story broke apart in 1986, when an
international row erupted over the hidden war

13
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:43,460
service of Kurt Waldheim,
then running for president.

14
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:49,120
In July 1991, Chancellor Franz
Vranitzky stood up in parliament and,

15
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:51,500
in effect, read out paragraph two.

16
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:56,100
We acknowledge all the deeds of our
history, and the deeds of all parts of our

17
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:58,320
people, the good as well as the evil.

18
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:01,080
And just as we claim the
good ones for ourselves,

19
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:03,680
we must apologise for the evil ones.
